  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.95,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings stop abruptly at about 0.50 from 4 h onward, straight after growth of about 2.4-fold per hour. That pattern suggests the reader maxes out around 0.5. Diluted retained aliquots confirmed this. At 18 h, the 10x dilution read 0.1888 and 0.1975 (about 1.93 after correcting for dilution), and the 40x dilution read 0.0493 (about 1.97). The two dilutions agree, so the reader responds proportionally at these low readings, and the true OD at 18 h is about 1.95, roughly four times the undiluted 0.506. At 10 h, the 10x dilution read 0.1785 (about 1.79) against an undiluted 0.518, so biomass kept rising during the apparent plateau. At 4 h, the 10x dilution read 0.058 (about 0.58) against an undiluted 0.482, so the reader was already under-reading there. The undiluted readings from about 4 to 18 h are capped by the reader and underestimate biomass. The diluted readings at 10 h and 18 h are single or duplicate reads, but their agreement makes the conclusion robust."
  },
